                    <div class="card border-2 border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-8">
                        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-red-700 mb-4 flex items-center">
                            <span class="text-3xl mr-3">&#10060;</span> The Old Way (Bare Sclera)
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">The old method simply scrapes the pterygium off, leaving the white of the eye &quot;bare&quot; to heal. This &quot;invites&quot; the growth to return, often more aggressively.</p>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                            <li class="flex"><span class="font-bold text-red-600 mr-2">&#10007;</span> <strong>High Recurrence Rate (up to 50%)</strong></li>
                            <li class="flex"><span class="font-bold text-red-600 mr-2">&#10007;</span> Can leave unsightly scarring</li>
                            <li class="flex"><span class="font-bold text-red-600 mr-2">&#10007;</span> Requires stitches, leading to irritation</li>
