        <section id="faq" class="py-20 bg-white">
            <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-3xl">
                <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-center text-teal-700 mb-12">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <div class="space-y-4">
                    <div class="faq-item bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border border-gray-200">
                        <div class="faq-question flex justify-between items-center p-5">
                            <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Is the pterygium surgery painful?</h4>
                            <span class="faq-arrow text-2xl text-teal-600">&#9660;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="faq-answer p-5 pt-0">
                            <p class="text-gray-600">No. Your eye is completely numbed with powerful anesthetic drops before and during the procedure. You will feel no pain, only light pressure. Any post-procedure discomfort is mild and easily managed with over-the-counter pain relievers.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border border-gray-200">
                        <div class="faq-question flex justify-between items-center p-5">
                            <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">What is the recovery time?</h4>
                            <span class="faq-arrow text-2xl text-teal-600">&#9660;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="faq-answer p-5 pt-0">
                            <p class="text-gray-600">Most patients are back to work and light activities within 2-3 days. You will wear an eye patch for the first 24 hours. The eye will be red and healing for 2-4 weeks, which is completely normal. After this healing phase, the redness subsides and the eye becomes clear and white.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border border-gray-200">
                        <div class="faq-question flex justify-between items-center p-5">
                            <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Is this covered by my insurance?</h4>
                            <span class="faq-arrow text-2xl text-teal-600">&#9660;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="faq-answer p-5 pt-0">
                            <p class="text-gray-600">It depends. If the pterygium is large enough to cause growth-induced astigmatism or obscure your vision, it is often considered medically necessary and covered by insurance. If it is purely for cosmetic reasons, it is typically an out-of-pocket procedure. We will help you determine this at your free consultation.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
